	(text "EoS TM4C1294 Board, rev A, two BoosterPack-compatible (40-pin) sites, 98-hole breakout, 10/100 Ethernet.\nDesigned by Kartikeydheer Srivastava.\nCopyright (c) 2026 Kartikeydheer Srivastava. All rights reserved; see LICENSE.txt.\nValues from TI SPMS433B (TM4C1294NCPDT), SPMA056 and SPMZ850G; Silicon Labs CP2102N Rev. 1.5; TI SLVSFG1A,\nSLVSDG1C, SLVSAC2G, SLVSDW8B; Littelfuse SP05xxBA and 1206L; Wurth 7499010121A; NDK NX3225GA; Abracon ABS07;\nCoilcraft XAL4000; Nexperia BAT54J; Kingbright.\nFirmware: OSCDRV = 1 (C25/C26 20 pF); USB as a forced device, VBUS on PB1; PD7 is NMI-locked.\nHIB switches ETH_VTERM (termination and centre taps) off in hibernation (SPMS433B 7.3.9).\nJP1/JP2: 1-2 + 3-4 = UART0 to the bridge, PD4/PD5 on BP2 A.5/A.6; 1-3 + 2-4 = CAN0 on BP2, bridge on UART2.\nBudget: 5 V pins + 0.75 x 3.3 V pins <= 300 mA in all. 3.3 V and 5 V header pins are outputs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330 130 0)
		(effects
